/*
 REFLECTIVE DASHBOARD - Waveshare ESP32-S3-RLCD-4.2

 BUILD
 - Arduino libraries: U8g2 2.36.18 / 2.36.19, ArduinoJson 7.4.3.
 - ESP32 board package: 3.3.11. Board: ESP32S3 Dev Module.
 - Flash: 16 MB; PSRAM: OPI; USB CDC On Boot: Enabled;
   USB Mode: Hardware CDC and JTAG; Flash: QIO, 80 MHz.
 - Partition: "16M Flash (3MB APP/9.9MB FATFS)" (app3M_fat9M_16MB).
 - Leave CPU menu at 240 MHz; firmware selects 80 MHz at runtime.
 - Open this INO from its same-named folder. Everything is in this one file.

 CONTROLS AND SETUP
 - KEY click: next page. BOOT click: previous page.
 - KEY hold (0.9 s): detail/graph, next aircraft or eligible refresh.
 - BOOT hold (2.5 s): open/close setup. PWR retains its hardware function.
 - Connect to RLCD-Setup-XXXX, using the setup code displayed on the LCD.
   Open http://192.168.4.1; username admin, password the same setup code.
 - Save home Wi-Fi first. Reopen setup to search an address, select a match,
   Use this location, review the nearby stop, then Save settings.
 - Setup closes after 10 minutes, except during a bounded active OTA upload.
 - OTA: Sketch > Export Compiled Binary, then upload ReflectiveDashboard.ino.bin
   in setup. Use the same board/partition settings and stable power. Do not
   upload merged, bootloader or partition binaries. Saved settings are retained.

 PAGES AND DATA
 - Home: date/time, next five hourly forecasts, local temperature and humidity.
   Hourly cells show time, day/night icon, temperature and rain probability.
   +1 marks tomorrow; times use the configured clock timezone.
 - Weather: three-day forecast; KEY hold switches to local sensor history.
 - Transport: PID / Golemio departures; free API key required:
   https://api.golemio.cz/api-keys. Offline stop list: PID snapshot 2026-09-14.
 - Aircraft: ADSB.lol positions (ODbL), adsbdb callsign route matches, 10 s
   carousel. Routes are not confirmed live itineraries. Missing callsigns and
   database gaps are shown explicitly. Temporary failures retry with backoff.
   Route data attribution: David Taylor and Jim Mason via adsbdb.
 - Forecast: Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0; free API for non-commercial use. Address
   search: Photon / komoot, OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).
 - News: direct HTTPS RSS 2.0; default BBC Europe, once per hour.
 - System: network, RTC, voltage-based battery estimate and diagnostics.

 HARDWARE AND OPERATION
 - LCD: ST7305, 300x400 native / 400x300 landscape; no backlight.
 - SHTC3 0x70 and PCF85063 0x51: SDA13, SCL14. KEY18, BOOT0, battery ADC4.
 - RTC stores UTC; POSIX timezone controls local time and DST. NTP every 6 h.
 - MCU sleep stays disabled for display stability; Wi-Fi stops between batches.
   Only changed display strips are sent. Audio amplifier remains disabled.
 - Sensor heat bias and charging affect measurements; battery % is an estimate.
 - Cached data survives network failures, not restart. STALE marks old/error data.
 - HTTPS verifies certificates and requires valid time; responses capped at 64 KB.
 - For USB recovery, hold BOOT while reconnecting USB, release, then upload.
 - Main battery: 18650. RTC backup must use the rechargeable type Waveshare specifies.

 FILE MAP
 1. Includes and Waveshare display adapter.
 2. Dashboard: configuration, sensors, drawing, networking, setup and OTA.
 3. Arduino setup()/loop().
 4. Appendix A: offline stop catalogue (bulk data, normally no edits needed).
 5. Appendix B: original display-adapter license (comment only, not firmware data).

 THIRD-PARTY CODE
 The ST7305 adapter is adapted from Waveshare's official example:
 https://github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-RLCD-4.2

 v1.4.0: five-hour home outlook with day/night icons and validated hourly data.
*/

